{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"3f50d1bf8eded81addbc6ac4f8468adf82bf37b7b3e56aa11d97ce3a21c09250","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_9ccc85ebf01694732eaa36304828b82861a0709359cddec72da8bb3c39fec220","overall_assessment":"The paper is generally well-organized and clearly written, with a logical flow from problem definition to methodology and results. The notation is consistent, and the algorithmic presentation is clear. The main clarity weakness lies in the inconsistent naming of specific adversarial methods (e.g., 'step 1.l.' vs 'step 1.1') and the lack of explicit axis definitions for the figures, which are described only in the caption text.","paper_id":"BJm4T4Kgx","paper_identity_sha256":"1776927d40fbcef251ea3c3bbad00b58516b7c34e4f28300100102377d9c8f2c","prompt_identity_sha256":"9d5c2864250e53e2880f510ca4d62e2d40bab7b2144275838bd2defdfced76d3","raw_response_sha256":"8185f157969870bdc702e690c4762b931443ef668edb164392f044979bb205ac","request_identity_sha256":"248845b2c856317cadd91df27d118db998be24cb0f07cfb9583b7bb82595166d","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"f0c1b6e5f5554b16f648d1796c97a3329a9fe0059b455d247cf73f07d0e07551","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-018","SRC-020","SRC-021"],"review_text":"The paper is well-structured with a clear narrative flow from introduction to conclusion. The terminology is generally precise, and the algorithm presentation in Algorithm 1 is self-contained and easy to follow. However, there is a notable inconsistency in the naming of the 'one-step least likely class' method. It is introduced as 'step 1.l.' (using a lowercase L) in Section 2.2, but is frequently referred to as 'step 1.1' (using the digit 1) in the results sections (e.g., Table 1 and Table 2 captions). This inconsistency can cause confusion for readers trying to map the method names to the results. Additionally, the paper states that a detailed comparison of one-step methods is omitted for brevity and refers to Appendix A, but this appendix is not included in the provided text, which limits the reader's ability to fully verify the claims made in the main text.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-007","SRC-008","SRC-012","SRC-014"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined. Section 2.1 provides a clear list of symbols and their meanings, which is helpful for the reader. The equations for the attack methods (FGSM, one-step target class, iterative methods) are clearly presented and the variables are defined. The loss function for adversarial training is also clearly defined with all parameters (m, k, lambda) explained. The notation for the clipping operation is well-defined. There are no significant issues with the mathematical presentation.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-019","SRC-021","SRC-024","SRC-026","SRC-031","SRC-033"],"review_text":"The tables (Tables 1-4) are well-structured and the data is clearly presented. The captions for the tables are informative and provide context for the results. However, the captions for Figure 1 and Figure 2 do not explicitly define the axes of the plots. For example, the caption for Figure 1 mentions 'Influence of size of the model on top 1 classification accuracy' but does not specify what the horizontal and vertical axes represent in terms of units or specific metrics (e.g., 'scale factor rho' on the x-axis and 'accuracy ratio' on the y-axis). The text in Section 4.3 mentions that the ratio of accuracy on adversarial images to accuracy on clean images is used as a measure of robustness, but this is not explicitly stated in the figure caption. Similarly, the caption for Figure 2 does not specify the axes. This makes it difficult for the reader to interpret the figures without referring back to the main text.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"b67a5a511a12cba4cb4dfe6fcdf3b0cb8527751af7ac6134e7bd07cadbd29f2f","paper_id":"BJm4T4Kgx","paper_ordinal":37,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"8185f157969870bdc702e690c4762b931443ef668edb164392f044979bb205ac","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJm4T4Kgx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"93f4c48508a0f69d13553aac98b9495b92e07d31d9617579fddb2819c2222459","request_identity_sha256":"248845b2c856317cadd91df27d118db998be24cb0f07cfb9583b7bb82595166d","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":868,"prompt_tokens":19119,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19987},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"248845b2c856317cadd91df27d118db998be24cb0f07cfb9583b7bb82595166d","role":"CLAR","role_ordinal":1,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}